Here's a simple HTML website that displays a random joke from a list of 4 jokes when a user clicks a button:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Random Joke Generator</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            text-align: center;
            padding-top: 100px;
        }
        button {
            padding: 10px 20px;
            font-size: 16px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        #joke {
            margin-top: 30px;
            font-size: 18px;
            color: #333;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Random Joke Generator</h1>
    <button onclick="showRandomJoke()">Tell Me a Joke</button>
    <div id="joke"></div>

    <script>
        const jokes = [
            "Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!",
            "What do you call fake spaghetti? An impasta!",
            "Why did the scarecrow win an award? Because he was outstanding in his field!",
            "What do you get when you cross a snowman and a vampire? Frostbite!"
        ];

        function showRandomJoke() {
            const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * jokes.length);
            document.getElementById('joke').textContent = jokes[randomIndex];
        }
    </script>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works:
- The HTML contains a button and a div to display the joke.
- The JavaScript defines an array of 4 jokes.
- When the button is clicked, the `showRandomJoke()` function is called.
- This function picks a random joke from the array and displays it in the `#joke` div.

You can copy this code into a `.html` file and open it in your browser to see it in action!

